<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Lantarón</h1><p class="st-meta">897 CE – 950 CE (approx.) · capital Lantarón</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small frontier county of the Kingdom of Asturias and León in the Ebro gorges, between Castile and Álava.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Lantarón, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> gorges on the borders of Álava and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgos">Burgos</a>, became a county at the end of the 9th century, when Count Gonzalo Téllez is recorded as ruling Lantarón and Cerezo. It was one of several frontier counties defending the eastern flank of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-asturias">Kingdom of Asturias</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The counts were military governors for the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> and León, holding castles such as Cerezo against raids from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banu-qasi">Banu Qasi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>. The population of the area was a mix of Basque and Romance speakers living in small villages.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 930s the county was absorbed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernan-gonzalez-of-castile">Fernán González</a> into the growing <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-castile">County of Castile</a>, and Lantarón ceased to be a separate county.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 897 CE – 950 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:77.55%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>897 CE – 950 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lantarón</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gonzalo Téllez</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Spain</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>County of Lantarón and Cerezo</dd></dl></aside></div>
